presence_conference Module
==========================

Overview
--------

The presence_conference module implements the SIP conference event package
(RFC 4575): it answers SUBSCRIBE requests for "Event: conference" and sends
NOTIFY bodies of type application/conference-info+xml describing the live
participant roster of a conference.

It is designed to run on the IMS MMTel-AS, which acts as the conference focus
(RFC 4579 section 4.4 / 3GPP TS 24.147). The actual media mixing is performed by
a FreeSWITCH MRF (MRFP); this module sources the roster from the mixer over the
FreeSWITCH Event Socket Library (ESL) using the `freeswitch` module's API.

The module registers a presence event ("conference") with a build_notify_body
callback (used for the initial and refresh NOTIFY) and an aux_body_processing
callback (used to patch the per-watcher monotonic "version" attribute). Live
roster updates are pushed to existing watchers via the presence
notify_all_on_publish() API, driven by the FreeSWITCH conference::maintenance
event (wired in the OpenSIPS script through the freeswitch_scripting module's
E_FREESWITCH event_route, which calls conference_notify()).

Dependencies
------------

  * presence
  * freeswitch
  * libxml2 (build dependency)

The presence module must be configured with a db_url (handle_subscribe()
requires the presentity / active_watchers / watchers tables).

Parameters
----------

  mrf_esl_url (string)
      FreeSWITCH ESL URL of the MRF, used to run "conference xml_list".
      Format: fs://[[user]:password@]host[:port]
      Example: "fs://:ClueCon@my-mrf:8021"
      If unset, rosters are served empty.

      The module lists all mixer conferences and matches the one whose name
      equals the focus URI conference id (comparing the part before any '@'),
      so it is robust to FreeSWITCH naming the conference "<id>",
      "<id>@default" or "<id>@<domain>".

  conf_user_prefix (string, default "conf=")
      User-part prefix that identifies a conference focus URI
      (sip:conf=<id>@conf-factory...). The conference id is the user part with
      this prefix stripped.

  default_expires (integer, default 3600)
      Default subscription expiry for the conference event.

Functions
---------

  conference_notify(presentity)
      Rebuild the roster for the given focus presentity URI from the MRF mixer
      and send a NOTIFY to every active watcher. Intended to be called from
      event_route[E_FREESWITCH] on conference::maintenance events.

Privacy
-------

Participants whose caller identity is restricted (CLIR, TS 24.147 / TS 24.607)
are anonymized in the roster (entity sip:anonymous@anonymous.invalid, no
display name). Detection is heuristic, based on the caller-id rendered by
FreeSWITCH.
